  "correctness_argument": "Three released conditions could not be stated by Environment, so the loaders dropped them (#1045). (1) Lamoureux 2023 leaves the oxygen regime blank on 178 of 1,035 PRECISE-1K samples ('Electron Acceptor', metadata_qc.csv sha256 68a0c5aa...) and on 250 of 1,675 public K-12 samples ('aerobicity', k12_modulome/metadata_qc.csv sha256 3904fb6d...). Environment.aerobicity was a required str defaulting to 'aerobic', so the only expressions were a guessed 'aerobic' or a drop. It is now a value or a typed ProvenanceGap: None only beside a ProvenanceGap(field='aerobicity') (the _aerobicity_stated_or_gapped validator, through _require_value_or_gap), the same contract Media's labels took in #901-#903. A None without the gap is refused and a gap beside a value is refused, so no record the old contract refused is accepted silently. (2) 15 public samples read 'transition', an oxygen regime that changes during the culture. The aerobicity vocabulary (a str validated against a fixed set) gains the member 'transition'; this is a vocabulary member addition (policy rule 7, enum_member_added in substance), which the impact tool reports only as 'validator/serializer changed' because the vocabulary is a validator set and not an Enum. It changes no existing value's meaning. 52 public samples read 'aerobic(30% DO)': the regime is 'aerobic' and the 30 % dissolved-oxygen setpoint is an EnvironmentPhysicalPerturbation of the new PhysicalFactor member 'dissolved_oxygen' with Concentration(30, percent) and a typed gap on the realizing agent, the pH precedent (a controlled physical setpoint with its released value and unit), so it is queryable rather than free text. (3) Schmidt 2016's two starved arms ('Starved cells were continuously shaken after reaching stationary phase for either 1 or 3 d') share medium, carbon source, temperature and oxygen regime with the exponential Glucose arm; the phase and the time held in it are what differ. Environment gains the optional growth_phase (the existing CultureGrowthPhase vocabulary, moved above Environment verbatim), set to 'stationary' beside duration_hours 24 and 72. It is excluded from the dump when None (the Genotype.natural_isolate precedent), so every environment that does not state it serializes exactly as before: the adapter tests that pin the yeast outputs and the content-addressed experiment, genotype and publication ids (test_bacterial_graph_classes, test_cell_adapter, test_ohya2005_adapter) pass unchanged. Every existing environment states an aerobicity from the old vocabulary, so it validates unchanged and dumps the same bytes. The contract fingerprints of Environment and PhysicalFactor still move, so every served closure that holds them re-stales and the change lands with the KG 4.0 full rebuild.",
  "measurement_type_decision": false,
